## 1. Executive Summary

PDF documents utilizing standard security handlers rely on symmetric ciphers to encrypt content streams, while delegating user credential validation to cryptographic hash digests stored within the file's trailer dictionary. 

This project conducted a security assessment against three password-locked target documents. Using offline cryptanalysis and dictionary-based techniques, the authentication signatures were extracted, parsed, and cracked. The recovered keys were subsequently validated by authenticating to each document and extracting its embedded competition flag

